      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the integral of $2{x}^{7/3}-\\frac{1}{3x}$ with respect to $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{7/3}-\\frac{1}{3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{x}^{7/3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{7/3+1}}{(\\frac{7}{3}+1)}-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{10/3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
